MID_SE_Max_Gol_C: <EDH>
MID_SE_Max_Gol_C_001: Ughhh. World, please...stop spinning.
MID_SE_Max_Gol_C_002: Ever since he told me those stories last night, it's\nbeen all I can do to keep my food down...
MID_SE_Max_Gol_C_003: Hey, Jester! You slept in, huh? Feelin' OK?
MID_SE_Max_Gol_C_004: Hey, Goliath...
MID_SE_Max_Gol_C_005: You're looking pretty wobbly! You good to stand?
MID_SE_Max_Gol_C_006: Oh yeah, I'm great. Never better.
MID_SE_Max_Gol_C_007: You can always tell your big brother if you're not\nfeeling good! I wanna help!
MID_SE_Max_Gol_C_008: How 'bout today, you get back in bed and try\ncatching some z's?
MID_SE_Max_Gol_C_009: And while you're dozing off, I can tell you\nanother story!
MID_SE_Max_Gol_C_010: No! No more stories!
MID_SE_Max_Gol_C_011: Huh? But you got so into the ones I told last night!\nHad this big, wide-eyed look on your face.
MID_SE_Max_Gol_C_012: Sorry, Goliath. That wasn't because I liked them.\nI was physically ill.
MID_SE_Max_Gol_C_013: I don't do well with stories about violence—especially\nwhile I'm trying to eat dinner.
MID_SE_Max_Gol_C_014: Oh! Huh!
MID_SE_Max_Gol_C_015: I didn't interrupt because I didn't want to be rude.\nBut all the blood rushed out of my head... Urp...
MID_SE_Max_Gol_C_016: Which one didn't you like? The time I strangled the\nbull? The time I snapped that guy's fingers?
MID_SE_Max_Gol_C_017: Ughhh. Please stop... Everything's spinning again.
MID_SE_Max_Gol_C_018: Huh, sorry! You're so good in a fight, I didn't take\nyou for the squeamish type.
MID_SE_Max_Gol_C_019: Well, guess I'll head home, then. Sleep tight!
MID_SE_Max_Gol_C_020: Thanks...
MID_SE_Max_Gol_C_021: He took it well enough. But why does that guy rub\nme the wrong way?
MID_SE_Max_Gol_C_022: So big and crass and violent. Maybe it's best I keep\nmy distance.
MID_SE_Max_Gol_B: <EDH>
MID_SE_Max_Gol_B_001: Aw, that all you're eating? You need more meat!\nHere, take some of mine.
MID_SE_Max_Gol_B_002: Blech... This is all fat!
MID_SE_Max_Gol_B_003: Now, just gonna stitch this up... Hahaha. Gotta have\nit ready for the dance of death!
MID_SE_Max_Gol_B_004: Hey! You mend your own clothes? I didn't know you\ndid that!
MID_SE_Max_Gol_B_005: Sounds fun. Here, let me help!
MID_SE_Max_Gol_B_006: Hey, easy with that! You know how strong you are!
MID_SE_Max_Gol_B_025: Guh, see? You ripped it!
MID_SE_Max_Gol_B_007: Hey, Jester! How ya doin'? Anything I can\nhelp with?
MID_SE_Max_Gol_B_008: You gotta be yanking my chain. When the HELL\nhave you ever helped?
MID_SE_Max_Gol_B_009: You're always getting in my way! You trying to piss\nme off and get stabbed in the neck?
MID_SE_Max_Gol_B_010: Huh? No, I was worried about you.
MID_SE_Max_Gol_B_011: I ain't a child! I get it, you think I'm sooo weak\ncompared to you.
MID_SE_Max_Gol_B_012: You act all worried, but you hate me! You're making\nfun of me! You think I'm a little runt!
MID_SE_Max_Gol_B_013: Wha?! Why would I think that? I got a lotta respect\nfor you!
MID_SE_Max_Gol_B_014: You...what?
MID_SE_Max_Gol_B_015: I joined the arena 'cause I was good at fighting.\nKicking, punching, smashing, squishing...
MID_SE_Max_Gol_B_016: The folks in my village hated me, so I had nothing\nelse to do anyway.
MID_SE_Max_Gol_B_017: Not you, though! There are lotsa other things you're\ngood at.
MID_SE_Max_Gol_B_018: You don't even like fighting, but you do it anyway—\nand do it good too!
MID_SE_Max_Gol_B_019: What you're doin' is hard. So, as your big brother,\nI'm just trying to make it easier.
MID_SE_Max_Gol_B_020: Hell... Starting to feel like a fool for gettin' so mad.
MID_SE_Max_Gol_B_021: Not a fool. You're smart, Jester.
MID_SE_Max_Gol_B_022: I guess... Gah, damn it! Are you expecting me to\nthank you, crap for brains?
MID_SE_Max_Gol_B_023: No. Wait, were you gonna?
MID_SE_Max_Gol_B_024: Shut it!
MID_SE_Max_Gol_A: <EDH>
MID_SE_Max_Gol_A_001: Haaah...
MID_SE_Max_Gol_A_002: Hey, Jester... Nah, I should stop getting in your way.
MID_SE_Max_Gol_A_003: Come on over, Goliath. Weird seeing a big guy like\nyou shrink back.
MID_SE_Max_Gol_A_004: Are you sure? You got mad about me messing\nwith you...
MID_SE_Max_Gol_A_005: Then don't mess with me. It's just too quiet in here—\nthe silence makes me want to kill someone.
MID_SE_Max_Gol_A_006: Tell me a story while I'm sewing. Might help drown\nout the thoughts.
MID_SE_Max_Gol_A_007: Uh! Sure! Happy to do it.
MID_SE_Max_Gol_A_008: Oh, but the only stories I can think of are me\nbeating people up. You hate those.
MID_SE_Max_Gol_A_009: It's fine. Better than fine. I want to hear one of your\nviolent stories.
MID_SE_Max_Gol_A_010: It's how I can stand up to that weakling living under\nmy mask.
MID_SE_Max_Gol_A_011: Besides, I kinda appreciate... Well, I don't mind you.
MID_SE_Max_Gol_A_012: You're a good guy, you know that?
MID_SE_Max_Gol_A_013: You too... To be honest, I didn't like you when I\nmet you. So big and loud and crude.
MID_SE_Max_Gol_A_014: I think that was the other guy coming through—\nthe delicate little squire-boy.
MID_SE_Max_Gol_A_015: Hey, fine by me! Only natural to rebel against your\nbig brother.
MID_SE_Max_Gol_A_016: Heh heh HEH! Always with the brother talk! The\nButcher and the Infernal Clown, a family.
MID_SE_Max_Gol_A_017: Pretty messed-up-sounding family. I kinda like it!
MID_SE_Max_Gol_A_018: Me too! OK, OK. Time for me to tell you a story.\nI've been sitting on this one!
MID_SE_Max_Gol_A_019: Ohoho! Let's hear it!
MID_SE_Max_Gol_A_020: So his nose was broke, and you know how when you\nbreak a guy's nose, it gets hard for him to breathe?
MID_SE_Max_Gol_A_021: He's all, HGEEH HNNNG. And then I gave him a\ncrack in the head! Boy, he was BLEEDING.
MID_SE_Max_Gol_A_022: Good thing to watch for, actually—guys with twisted\nnoses. That means they've had their clocks cleaned!
MID_SE_Max_Gol_A_023: Eughhh...
MID_SE_Max_Gol_A_024: Hey, Jester? You been pretty quiet! Liking the story?
MID_SE_Max_Gol_A_025: Jester!
MID_SE_Max_Gol_A_026: Hey! What happened to standing up to yourself?!